# Always push an OTA update after shipping changes

After committing any change that affects the native app's JS bundle or assets,
push an OTA update to the `production` channel without being asked.

```bash
NODE_OPTIONS="--max-old-space-size=8192" yarn eas update \
  --channel production \
  --message "<short summary of the change>" \
  --non-interactive
```

`NODE_OPTIONS` is required — the default ~2 GB Node heap makes `expo export`
die with "JavaScript heap out of memory" partway through serializing this
bundle.

Report the update group ID and the EAS dashboard URL when it completes.

## What OTA cannot ship

OTA only replaces the JS bundle and assets. These need a full `eas build` and
store submission instead, so call it out rather than pushing an OTA:

- `app.json` native config: plugins, permissions, `scheme`, icons, splash
- Added/removed/upgraded native modules in `package.json`
- Any change to `runtimeVersion` (currently `6.0.8` in app.json). Store
  binaries only install OTAs whose runtime matches **exactly**:
  - iOS App Store 6.0.11 → runtime `6.0.8` (and publish `6.0.11` as well)
  - Play Android last approved FGS-stripped binaries → runtime `6.0.7`
  - Newer Play/iOS binaries (build 177+) → runtime `6.0.8`

Until those older binaries are gone, publish every runtime after the default:

```bash
EAS_UPDATE_RUNTIME_VERSION=6.0.11 NODE_OPTIONS="--max-old-space-size=8192" yarn eas update \
  --channel production \
  --message "<short summary> (runtime 6.0.11)" \
  --non-interactive

EAS_UPDATE_RUNTIME_VERSION=6.0.7 NODE_OPTIONS="--max-old-space-size=8192" yarn eas update \
  --channel production \
  --message "<short summary> (runtime 6.0.7)" \
  --non-interactive
```

## Channels

`production` is the live channel used by store builds. Use `preview` or
`development` only when the change is explicitly for internal testing.
